  "description": "A parametric FLOOR LAMP on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nTHE SHADE MOVES, WHICH IS WHAT AN ARC LAMP IS. Set the style to Arc and the shade's centre slides out by the reach while the base stays put — so the plan shows the shade over the sofa and the base beside it, which is the entire reason someone buys one. Column and Tripod leave the reach at zero.\n\nTWO RINGS AND A STEM. The shade and the base are 24-point rings, because a drum shade drawn as a square is wrong in the one view where a lamp is mostly shade. The stem, the arc arm and the tripod legs are quad rows on the shared table.\n\nREACH IS PUBLISHED separately from the footprint, because the footprint is the base and the reach is where the light actually lands — and on an arc lamp those are a metre apart.",
